      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:6:132:8",
      "text": [
        " لَا تَخَلَّلُوا بِعُودِ الرَّيْحَانِ وَ لَا بِقَضِيبِ الرُّمَّانِ فَإِنَّهُمَا يُهَيِّجَانِ عِرْقَ الْجُذَامِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Ibrahim Bin Abdul Hameed, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Do not pick teeth with a stem of basil, nor with a stem of the pomegranate, for these two agitate the vein of leprosy’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "8. Ali has narrated from Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from Yunus ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman from those whom he has mentioned who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘If one uses reeds as toothpicks none of his wishes can come true for six days.’” "
        ]
      }
